  "label": "Stereotype: Indigenous women are crazy or hysterical",
  "description": "This is a harmful racial and gender stereotype that portrays Indigenous women as emotionally unstable, irrational, or violent. It is used to demean and dehumanize them, reducing their complex identities to a simplistic, irrational caricature. This stereotype is rooted in historical racism and misogyny against Indigenous peoples, particularly women, and is often used to justify systemic discrimination and violence.",
